ut that if the  final records archived and used to  demonstrate batch quality to the FDA are  stored in paper format then the 21 CFR  part 11 rule does not apply to any  computer even to the computer used to  generate the paper records in the first  place ie if the final record is kept in  paper format and not electronic format  then the 21 CFR part 11 rule does not  apply so now let's take a look at why  online TOC analyzers have taken on an  increased importance in September of  2004 the FDA issued their process  analytical technology guidance  encouraging the pharmaceutical industry  to change their reliance on the final  product testing and to employee more  online process monitoring in an attempt  to get a better process understanding  and process control leading to improved  right first time quality results  online monitoring particularly for TOC  on conductivity have taken on even  greater significance since the European  pharmacopoeia adopted its revised  monograph on water for injection in  March of 2016 allowing for the first  time the generation of water for  injection from reverse osmosis the  working group responsible for advising  the European Directorate on their new  water injection monograph gave a warning  that reverse osmosis may not be as  robust as stills and they encouraged a  focus on online TOC and conductivity  monitoring as early warning indicates  the potential reverse osmosis integrity  breaches so now let's take a look at  what other guidance the FDA gives on the  topic of quality control records and  data integrity in their 2003 documents  on the implementation of the 21 CFR part  11 data integrity rule the FDA issue so  use the acronym Alcoa where they define  good data integrity practices creating  records that are attributable to the  technician carrying out the testing  illegible are created contemporaneously  and they are the original record and  they are accurate in this case  attributable means that the record  should include an 